{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Our father died in the wilderness, and he was not.</b> etc. Ramban writes: according to my view by way of the plain sense (peshat), they said this because people thought that Moses our master, peace be upon him, hated the congregation of Korah more than all the other sinners who died in the wilderness, since they had been zealous against him and denied all his deeds, and they thought that perhaps in his hatred of them he would say (Psalms 109:12) ״אל יהי לו מושך חסד ואל יהי חונן ליתומיו״, ״יזכר עון אבותיו אל ה'״ — therefore they informed him that their father was not among them, and they further intimated that he was not among those who died in the plague but died in the wilderness upon his bed. End quote." "<b>For he died in his sin.</b> An individual sin, like the other individuals who sin. And they said in the name of R. Judah ha-Levi, of blessed memory, that ״כי בחטאו מת״ is joined with ״ובנים לא היו לו״ — as one would say today, 'because of sins such-and-such occurred.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:23.875401189Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}